+# Provisioning Runbook — KMS/CI OIDC, Rekor, ExternalSecrets, Presidio, Gatekeeper, Detector scaling & tests
+
+This runbook consolidates commands, order and checks to make the new moderation/PII/verification flows trustworthy.
+
+1) KMS signing & GitHub Actions OIDC (preferred)
+ - For AWS:
+   - Create a KMS asymmetric key or symmetric key with Sign permission.
+   - Run: ./scripts/setup_aws_oidc_kms.sh <github-org> <github-repo> <kms-key-arn> <role-name>
+   - In GitHub repo > Settings > Secrets > Actions, add:
+       - AWS_ROLE_ARN: arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_ID:role/<role-name>
+       - COSIGN_KMS_URI: aws-kms://arn:aws:kms:REGION:ACCOUNT_ID:key/<key-id>
+   - Configure GitHub Action to assume role via OIDC (see AWS docs).
+
+ - For GCP/Azure/Vault: create corresponding KMS keys and provide COSIGN_KMS_URI in GitHub Secrets. Use provider-specific instructions for OIDC or service account keys (prefer OIDC where supported).
+
+2) Rekor
+ - Deploy Rekor: kubectl apply -f k8s/rekor/deployment.yaml
+ - Expose Rekor (ClusterIP) or create Ingress for your domain; set REKOR_SERVER to "https://rekor.example.com" in GH Secrets.
+ - Verify: run cosign upload-blob --rekor-url $REKOR_SERVER --signature artifact.bin.sig artifact.bin from CI runner.
+
+3) ExternalSecrets
+ - Install operator: ./k8s/external-secrets/install_external_secrets.sh
+ - Apply the SecretStore that matches your provider:
+     kubectl apply -f external-secrets/secretstore-aws-secretsmanager.yaml
+     OR external-secrets/secretstore-gcp-secretmanager.yaml OR azure/vault
+ - Create ExternalSecret for MCP Postgres:
+     kubectl apply -f external-secrets/externalsecret-mcp-postgres.yaml
+
+4) Presidio deployment (PII)
+ - Deploy Presidio components and services:
+     kubectl apply -f k8s/presidio/presidio-deploy.yaml
+ - Confirm services are reachable:
+     kubectl -n presidio get svc
+ - The PII adapter expects PRESIDIO_ANALYZER env var reachable by services (e.g. http://presidio-analyzer:3000)
+
+5) Deploy detectors & verifier
+ - Build and push images (or use CI images).
+ - Deploy moderation & verifier to K8s:
+     kubectl apply -f k8s/moderation/moderation-deployment.yaml
+     kubectl apply -f k8s/verifier/verifier-deployment.yaml
+ - Add HPAs:
+     kubectl apply -f k8s/moderation/moderation-hpa.yaml
+     kubectl apply -f k8s/verifier/verifier-hpa.yaml
+ - Ensure nodeSelector/tolerations match your GPU node labels if using GPUs.
+
+6) Gatekeeper / OPA
+ - Install Gatekeeper:
+     ./k8s/gatekeeper/install_gatekeeper.sh
+ - Apply your ConstraintTemplate & Constraint (we included examples in repo).
+ - Test: create a Deployment without annotation mcp.provenance/signed=true and confirm Gatekeeper denies creation (tune rules as needed).
+
+7) Provenance completeness
+ - Ensure your CI uses .github/workflows/cosign_kms_rekor_all.yml (or equivalent) to sign artifacts and attempt Rekor upload.
+ - After sign step, run ./scripts/save_sig_to_s3.sh <artifact> <s3-bucket> to persist artifact & .sig.
+ - Ensure MCP ingestion or release pipelines store artifact URIs and signature URIs together.
+
+8) Safety & compliance
+ - Configure Presidio anonymizers to redact according to your policy. Validate redaction on sample PII data.
+ - Harden A2A approver: require auth (JWT/OAuth), persist approvals in DB, log ACCESSES.
+
+9) Testing & validation
+ - Local integration:
+    docker-compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml up --build
+    python scripts/load_test_detectors.py
+ - Red-team & adversarial tests:
+    - Prepare labeled corpora for NSFW/hallucination/PII.
+    - Run samples and measure false positives/negatives.
+ - Performance:
+    - Load test with load_test_detectors.py while scaling HPA and measuring p95/p99.
+
+10) Notes on scaling & cost
+ - NLI and Detoxify are heavy; consider smaller models or async verification paths for low-latency user flows.
+ - Use GPU node pools with autoscaler for bursty verification workloads.
+ - Vision moderation recommended via specialized model or cloud provider API for accuracy.
+
